    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4736" root="ثمن" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَامِنٌ</span></b>  [<i>Eighth:</i> fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>]. (S, K, &amp;c.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَامِنَ عَشَرَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَامِنَةَ عَشْرَةَ</span>, the former masc. and
the latter fem., meaning <i>Eighteenth,</i> are subject
to the same rules as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَالِثَ عَشَرَ</span> and its fem., explained in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثلث</span>, q. v.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ ثَوَامِنُ</span>, [the
latter word pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَامِنَةٌ</span>,] <i>Camels that come to
water on the eighth night</i> [<i>after the next preceding
watering</i>]: from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثِمْنٌ</span>. (TA.)

